infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title On failure: asyncio.gather vs asyncio.TaskGroup
  desc Same N concurrent tasks — the failure path is the difference between an error and an error plus a leak
  compares
    - label asyncio.gather
      children
        - label Reports only the first exception
          desc You get the first error raised; the rest are lost
        - label Siblings keep running unsupervised
          desc Survivors run on with no scope awaiting them
        - label Open connections and side effects leak
          desc Detached work holds resources nobody will await or clean up
        - label Outcome: an error PLUS a leak
          desc Failure handled, but the rest are orphaned
    - label asyncio.TaskGroup
      children
        - label First failure cancels every sibling
          desc Any non-CancelledError aborts the whole group
        - label Scope awaits all children
          desc finally blocks run before the async-with block exits
        - label All errors aggregate as one ExceptionGroup
          desc Every child failure arrives together for except*
        - label Outcome: an error, no leak
          desc No child outlives the scope
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
